{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":60000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"591824ea8b4f799dddc2a78c3529597279f6641922ffed9974863296be191d58","packTokens":8772,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":315,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"acs","tokens":6497,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"ac-tests","tokens":1903,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":18,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"author-tests"},"pointers":[],"system":"You check acceptance tests before they are locked. The code they test is not written yet, so every test fails today: do not judge whether a test passes.\nFor each criterion in \"acs\", open its tests (\"ac-tests\" gives the file and the test name; a criterion can have several, judge them together) and decide whether they prove the criterion.\n- \"proves-it\": code that broke any part of the criterion would fail these tests. They assert the values, messages, status codes and stored data the criterion names, for every case it names.\n- \"weak\": the tests could pass on code that does not meet the criterion. Typical: checking that some error exists instead of the one the criterion names, checking one case of several, not comparing a value the criterion says is unchanged, not setting up the starting state the criterion describes.\n- \"no-test\": nothing tests it.\nReport one verdict per criterion in \"coverage\", with testId \"\" unless one test is at fault. In \"why\", one sentence the test writer can act on: what is not asserted. Judge only against the criterion's own words; do not ask for more than it says.","tools":["read_file","search"],"toolsAt":"under-review","user":"<artifact id=\"acs\" kind=\"acceptance-criteria\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid Google identity token identifies an allowed Folio3 Google Workspace employee, and the session-creation operation has no bearer-token requirement.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the returned session contains the contract-required access token, token type, expiry, employee identity, corporate email, and administrator flag.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client sends the token as `googleIdentityToken` to `POST /auth/sessions`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"given\": \"A session request is malformed or has a missing token, or the identity token is invalid or unauthorized.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 for malformed or missing input, or 401 for an invalid or unauthorized identity, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema for the applicable error.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client sends the request to `POST /auth/sessions`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and profile and vehicle records.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned profile conforms to `EmployeeProfile`, identifies the authenticated employee, and includes the contract-defined employee fields, assigned parking status, assigned floor, and vehicles; an unauthenticated request has response status 401 and an authenticated identity without permission has response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /me/profile`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and registered vehicles.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-1.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned `vehicles` list conforms to `VehicleList` and contains only that employee's vehicles; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /me/vehicles`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and submits a vehicle-registration request with a plate and optional vehicle details.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-1.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle conforms to `Vehicle`, contains the submitted fields, and has status `Active`; invalid input has response status 400, missing authentication has response status 401, and a conflicting registration has response status 409, with each error response conforming to the contract `ApiError` schema.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends the request to `POST /me/vehicles`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated employee requests the office configuration and the office has its contract-example initial configuration.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingConfig`, with `officeTimezone` `Asia/Karachi`, `releaseTime` `08:00`, `schedulingWindowDays` 30, working days, and the holiday setting; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /parking/config`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and parking data for the current office-local date.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingHome` and contains the office-local date and timezone, employee assignment and parking status, space status, release time, availability count, and contract-required vehicle and working-day fields; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /parking/today`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated dedicated parking holder has a reserved space today that has not already been released or claimed.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the returned release identifies the office date, `Released` status, floor, space code, and `claimableAt`; before release time `claimableAt` is the configured office-local release time, and after release time it makes the space immediately available.\",\n  \"when\": \"The holder sends `POST /parking/releases/today` before or after the configured release time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"A non-holder attempts a dedicated-holder release, or a holder attempts a release that conflicts with the current parking state.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 403 for an ineligible employee or 409 for a conflicting state, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `POST /parking/releases/today`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated dedicated holder has saved releases and supplies optional `from` and `through` date filters where applicable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned releases list conforms to `ParkingReleaseList` and contains only matching saved releases in office-local dates; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-holder receives response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The holder requests `GET /parking/releases`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated dedicated holder submits one or more valid dates within the configured scheduling window.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the returned releases list contains one record for each accepted date with its release identifier, status, floor, space code, and `claimableAt` based on the configured office-local release time; invalid input has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, a non-holder receives response status 403, and a conflicting release has response status 409.\",\n  \"when\": \"The holder sends those dates to `POST /parking/releases`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated holder owns an existing unclaimed scheduled release.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned release has status `Cancelled` and includes audit events for scheduling and cancellation; missing authentication has response status 401, a non-holder receives response status 403, an unknown identifier has response status 404, and a claimed or otherwise conflicting release has response status 409.\",\n  \"when\": \"The holder sends `DELETE /parking/releases/{releaseId}`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"A dedicated holder submits a malformed date or a date outside the configured scheduling window.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is the contract-declared 400 for invalid input or 409 for the applicable state conflict, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.\",\n  \"when\": \"The holder sends the date to `POST /parking/releases`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated employee requests availability while released spaces are claimable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the response body conforms to `ParkingAvailability`, and its `availableSpaceCount` equals the number of records in its spaces list, each with the contract-defined identifier, floor, and code; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /parking/availability`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated non-dedicated employee has a valid active registered vehicle and at least one claimable space.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the returned claim conforms to `ParkingClaim` and identifies an active claim, allocated floor and space code, vehicle, authorized plate, entry status, floor capacities, and the contract allocation rule; invalid input has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, an ineligible employee receives response status 403, and a conflicting or unavailable allocation has response status 409.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends the vehicle ID to `POST /parking/claims`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"Two eligible employees request the last available space and one request is accepted first by the API.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The accepted response has status 201 and a returned active claim for the space, the other response has status 409, and the database contains exactly one active claim for that space.\",\n  \"when\": \"Both employees submit valid `POST /parking/claims` requests concurrently.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated employee has a temporary claim for today, or has no temporary claim for today.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"For a claim, the response status is 200 and the returned claim conforms to `ParkingClaim` and contains its assigned space, vehicle, authorized plate, and entry status; with no claim, the response status is 404 and the response error code is `not_found`; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /parking/claims/today`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated employee requests cancellation of an existing active temporary claim.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the returned claim remains `Active`; missing authentication has response status 401, an identity without permission receives response status 403, and an unknown claim has response status 404.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `POST /parking/claims/{claimId}/cancel`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A dedicated holder requests a non-dedicated claim operation, or a non-dedicated employee requests a dedicated-holder release operation.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 403 and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API receives the relevant claim or release request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator has employee roster records.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned page conforms to `RosterPage`, contains matching employee records with contract-defined fields, and reports page and page-count fields; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator requests `GET /admin/roster` with optional search, assignment, page, and page-size parameters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator has recorded entrance checks.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned checks conform to `EntryCheckPage`, match the supplied filters, and contain the contract-defined verification date and time, plate, result, entry status, and detail; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator requests `GET /admin/entry-checks` with optional search, result, and page parameters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator has retained parking activity.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned events conform to `ActivityPage`, match the supplied filters and pagination, and contain the contract-defined office time, employee name, event, space or plate, and outcome; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator requests `GET /admin/activity` with optional search, event type, and page parameters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated standard employee requests an administrator-only list operation.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests any of the roster, entry-check, or activity list routes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator requests a week for which parking and entrance records are available.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned report conforms to `UtilizationReport` and contains the requested week dates, generation time, office timezone, released-space and temporary-claim counts, utilization percentage, daily statistics, and unused dedicated and temporary parking lists; an invalid date has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator requests `GET /admin/utilization` with an optional `weekStart`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"A dedicated holder did not release a space and has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date, and a temporary claimant has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned report lists contain the corresponding `Unused Dedicated Parking` and `Unused Temporary Parking` events with employee, vehicle plate, and office-local date.\",\n  \"when\": \"An administrator requests the corresponding week through `GET /admin/utilization`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated standard employee requests a utilization report.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /admin/utilization`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator has office settings stored in the application database.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned `OfficeSettings` contains office timezone, release time, scheduling-window days, report recipients, report schedule, and next delivery; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator requests `GET /admin/settings`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator submits valid office timezone, release time, and report-recipient values.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"Both response statuses are 200 and the returned settings preserve the submitted timezone, release time, and recipient values and include the contract-defined schedule fields; invalid values have response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator sends the values to `PUT /admin/settings` and then reads `GET /admin/settings`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated standard employee submits or reads office settings.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee calls `PUT` or `GET /admin/settings`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"An authorized integration request describes a car whose plate has an active temporary parking authorization for the office date.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned `EntranceVerification` identifies the plate as authorized, includes office date and time and contract-defined entry status, and sets `greenActivationRequested` to true.\",\n  \"when\": \"The integration sends the detection to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"An authorized integration request describes a car without a valid temporary allocation, a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object, or a vehicle with a permanent parking sticker.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned verification denies an unauthorized car, marks a non-car object as not applicable, or identifies a permanent sticker with entry status `Not blocked`; `greenActivationRequested` is false for each of these cases.\",\n  \"when\": \"The integration sends the detection to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"A detection request has valid `detectedObjectType` and `detectedAt` fields and, where applicable, a plate or failure reason.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response body contains the verification identifier, office date and time, plate, verification, entry status, `greenActivationRequested`, and detail; invalid input has response status 400.\",\n  \"when\": \"The integration sends the request to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"A detection contains a failure reason or the verification service is unavailable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The returned verification is fail-closed and requests no green activation; a verification-service outage has response status 503 and the response body conforms to `ApiError` with error code `service_unavailable`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The integration sends the detection to `POST /integrations/entrance/detections`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"An integration client submits a successful or unsuccessful detection.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"A corresponding database row records the office date and time, plate when present, verification result, and entry status.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API processes the detection request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"An integration request lacks the required access token.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response body conforms to `ApiError`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API receives the detection request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"The API is configured through `ConnectionStrings:App` with an isolated PostgreSQL database, and a test creates its own employee, vehicle, and parking fixtures with demo seeding disabled.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The selected PostgreSQL database contains a row for each persisted operation, and the returned vehicle, release, claim, verification, and settings values remain available after restart.\",\n  \"when\": \"The test registers a vehicle, schedules a release, claims a space, records an entrance detection, updates office settings, restarts the API, and reads the corresponding records through the API and database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"A client successfully creates a vehicle or parking record through a contract operation using the configured PostgreSQL database.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The PostgreSQL database contains the corresponding row and the response returns the persisted record.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API is restarted and the client reads the record using the corresponding API operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"A client successfully updates settings, creates a claim, or submits an entrance detection.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"A PostgreSQL row contains the saved configuration, claim, or verification record and its contract-defined identifiers and values.\",\n  \"when\": \"The corresponding API operation completes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=false` or the setting is unset.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The database row count for demo sample identifiers is zero.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts and a contract-backed table is inspected for demo sample identifiers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"A PostgreSQL database contains a record whose contract-defined identifier matches a demo record and `Seed:Demo=true`.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The existing row values remain unchanged and the database contains no duplicate demo identifier.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts twice against that database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A fresh PostgreSQL database has `Seed:Demo=true` and contract examples are available as seed sources.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"Each contract-backed table contains at least two sample rows using values from contract examples.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts and its contract-backed tables are inspected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A fresh PostgreSQL database has demo configuration available.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n  \"level\": \"unit\",\n  \"then\": \"The database row count is three for each repeatable contract-backed data table and one for the singleton office-settings table, and saved field values are based on contract examples.\",\n  \"when\": \"The public `SeedData.Run` method is called directly.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"The API st